IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `bdm-registration`

-- Births, Deaths and Marriages Registration Act 1998 (Western Australia) -- s 44, the doctor's certificate of cause of death.
--
-- Edition, scope, sources and method: as in bdm-registration.l4, whose types this module uses. Written with the writing-l4-rules
-- skill; conformed to the writing-l4-rules skill on 14 October 2026, and to section 5 of docs/ENCODING-GUIDE.md (the stable l4,
-- 1.6.98) on 22 October 2026. YMD, `Why not covered` and `Answer` come from bdm-registration.l4. In the first pass s 44 was a
-- section of bdm-registration.l4; it
-- has its own module now only because its period is in HOURS and that module's clock is in days (the phrasebook, entry 4.3: one unit
-- per file).
--
-- THE CLOCK. Every WITHIN in this module, and every AT in a #TRACE of a rule in it, counts HOURS -- and only this comment says so.
-- AT 0 is the death; an act stamped n happened n hours after it. "Within 48 hours" is WITHIN 48, inclusive: hour 48 is in time.

§ `Births, Deaths and Marriages Registration Act 1998 -- s 44`

§§ `44 -- the doctor's certificate of cause of death`

-- s 44(1): the doctor responsible for the person's care immediately before death, or who examined the body, "must, within 48 hours
-- after the person's death -- (c) certify ... the cause of the death; and (d) give the certificate to the person who is responsible
-- under section 42". (2), (3) the same for a stillbirth and a neonatal death. Penalty: $1 000. (4): no offence if another doctor gives
-- it or "the doctor had reasonable cause for not being able to comply". (5): no certificate is required if the doctor must report the
-- death to a coroner under s 17(3) of the Coroners Act 1996. The certificate goes to the funeral director, not the Registrar.
--
-- Which doctor of (1)(a)/(b), (2)(a)/(b) or (3)(a)/(b) is `the doctor responsible under section 44` is the caller's fact; the three
-- subsections impose the same two acts in the same 48 hours, so one rule serves all three.
@ref Births, Deaths and Marriages Registration Act 1998 (WA) s 44(1)-(3), (5)
GIVEN d IS A Death
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a doctor must certify the cause of death` d IF
    NOT (d's `reportable to a coroner under section 17(3) of the Coroners Act 1996`)

-- THE DUTY. (c) and (d) are two acts in the same 48 hours: RAND, each with its own reason. A death reportable to a coroner is not a
-- case the Act leaves open -- (5) answers it: no certificate is required -- so it is FULFILLED, not `not covered`. This is the duty
-- as s 44 states it, the rule a #TRACE runs; a death before 14 April 1999 is the next rule's.
@ref Births, Deaths and Marriages Registration Act 1998 (WA) s 44(1)-(3), (5)
GIVEN d IS A Death
GIVETH A DEONTIC `A party under this Act` `An act under this Act`
`s 44 -- the doctor must certify the cause of death and give the certificate within 48 hours` d MEANS
    IF   NOT (`a doctor must certify the cause of death` d)
    THEN FULFILLED
    ELSE
                (PARTY  `the doctor responsible under section 44`
                 MUST   `certify the cause of the death`
                 WITHIN 48
                 HENCE  FULFILLED
                 LEST   BREACH BY `the doctor responsible under section 44`
                        BECAUSE "s 44(1)-(3)(c): the cause of the death was not certified within 48 hours after the death")
            RAND
                (PARTY  `the doctor responsible under section 44`
                 MUST   `give the certificate to the person responsible under section 42`
                 WITHIN 48
                 HENCE  FULFILLED
                 LEST   BREACH BY `the doctor responsible under section 44`
                        BECAUSE "s 44(1)-(3)(d): the certificate was not given to the person responsible under section 42 within 48 hours")

-- THE QUESTION. The s 44 duty for this death, or `not covered` for a death before 14 April 1999 (s 2).
@ref Births, Deaths and Marriages Registration Act 1998 (WA) s 2, s 44(1)-(3), (5)
GIVEN d IS A Death
GIVETH AN `Answer` (DEONTIC `A party under this Act` `An act under this Act`)
`s 44 -- the doctor's duty to certify, or why it is not covered` d MEANS
    IF   `the event was before the Act was in operation` (d's `date of the death`)
    THEN `not covered` `a registrable event before 14 April 1999 is governed by the law then in force, which is not encoded in this model`
    ELSE `answered` (`s 44 -- the doctor must certify the cause of death and give the certificate within 48 hours` d)

-- THE OFFENCE. Constitutive (entry 5.7). s 44(4) takes the offence away, not the duty, where another doctor gave the certificate or
-- the doctor had reasonable cause.
DECLARE `The doctor's certificate` HAS
    `hours after the death it was given`                                IS A NUMBER
    `given by another doctor`                                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `the doctor had reasonable cause for not being able to comply`      IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Births, Deaths and Marriages Registration Act 1998 (WA) s 44(1)-(4)
GIVEN d IS A Death
      c IS A `The doctor's certificate`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the doctor commits an offence under s 44` d c IF
        `a doctor must certify the cause of death` d
    AND (c's `hours after the death it was given` GREATER THAN 48)
    AND "(4)(a)" ... NOT (c's `given by another doctor`)
    AND "(4)(b)" ... NOT (c's `the doctor had reasonable cause for not being able to comply`)
